  "description": "is made from X-Fusion Alpha,\nnew aluminum alloy tubes that do not lose strength when welded. So a new\nTeam will be lighter and ride better than Teams of the past. That's saying\na lot, by the way.\n\nTeam frame geometry is exactly the same as the Mercury and 7UP Team Issue\nbikes. A Team will handle and steer just like those guys' bikes. Its parts\nare nearly the same too, because current Ultegra comes closer to Dura-Ace\nthan ever before.\n\nThis year's Team is spec'd with a full-carbon fork, meaning the steerer\ntube and crown are also carbon fiber. And: Ritchey bladed-spoke aero wheels,\na Ritchey seatpost and integrated headset, a titanium-rail saddle and\nVittoria Rubino Pro tires with Kevlar beads. Good raceable, trainable,\ncentury-rideable stuff.\n\nDrop by your Fuji dealer and take a look at a new Team. Re-read the specs\nand what I've said here. Ride a Team, a Team Super Lite and a couple of\nthe other guys' bikes. You'll know what to do.",
